                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
                        "entry_id": "6d97d851-fa45-3967-a73a-d198120dba2e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Branntwein aus Reis oder Melasse"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f732c518-aa55-431f-a59a-fc6b18297f49",
                                "sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
                                "text": "„So versorgten sie uns halbwegs mit Reis und Arrak, einigen Schweinen und sechs oder sieben lebenden Kühen und kamen, mit Vorräten beladen und mit dem Auftrag, dorthin zurückzukehren, wieder zu uns.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2c5ca35-595d-4822-ad60-44ed1e753dc4",
                                "sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
                                "text": "„Und aus dem Saft der Palmen ließ sich Wein machen oder ein rumartiger Schnaps namens Arrak brennen.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eed0e5bd-c9a7-4762-a2d4-5c72512c8673",
                                "sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
                                "text": "„Ich sagte ihm auch, ich wolle das nächstemal bittere Orangen haben, um dem Punsch Geschmack zu geben; außerdem wolle ich Rum und nicht Arrak.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "15101ec4-399b-408a-a1ee-950cc37b09f0",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d97d851-fa45-3967-a73a-d198120dba2e",
                        "source_sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Branntwein aus Reis oder Melasse",
                        "target_lang_word": "arrack",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "arrack",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "acd3f557-342c-397c-9ccb-19590cc3698b",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d40755-cded-32e2-af4f-f671d1f12d1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An alcoholic drink distilled from coconut palm flowers in South Asia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bef2ebf-d306-4fe8-8043-2f971e080186",
                                                "sense_id": "acd3f557-342c-397c-9ccb-19590cc3698b",
                                                "text": "From hence we firſt ſailed to Achin, in the iſland of Sumatra, and then to Siam, where we bartered our wares for ſome arrack and opium, the laſt of which bore a great price among the Chineſe:[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e94ea7d-9ac7-49ff-82f1-a99943040b4b",
                                                "sense_id": "acd3f557-342c-397c-9ccb-19590cc3698b",
                                                "text": "[…] the cocoa-nut tree yields a pure draught from a dry and barren land; a cup of water to the temperate and thirsty traveler; a cup of cream from the pressed kernel; a cup of refreshing and sparkling toddy to the early riser; a cup of arrack to the hardened spirit-drinker, and a cup of oil, by the light of which I now extol its merits—five separate and distinct liquids from the same tree!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51879283-ca31-48e9-9899-bdcccc226ed0",
                                                "sense_id": "acd3f557-342c-397c-9ccb-19590cc3698b",
                                                "text": "Ceylon teaches many lessons. The liquor traffic, for instance, is managed throughout the entire island as a governmental monopoly. […] Pure arrack only can be sold at fixed prices, and lessees are held to strict account for drunkenness and disturbances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa4c8411-39a0-4a56-950f-9bce6bcaf167",
                                                "sense_id": "acd3f557-342c-397c-9ccb-19590cc3698b",
                                                "text": "Moti Guj was very fond of liquor—arrack for choice, though he would drink palm-tree toddy if nothing better offered."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "baecaae2-a831-4094-bc3e-c67e55440ddb",
                                                "sense_id": "acd3f557-342c-397c-9ccb-19590cc3698b",
                                                "text": "The Moh tree, botanically Bassia Latifolia, produces flowers rich in sugar, used in India in the manufacture of the liquor arrack."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60a3ce98-f305-3be2-b33a-6d2438a7e445",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d40755-cded-32e2-af4f-f671d1f12d1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An alcoholic drink made from sugar cane and fermented red rice in Indonesia."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4544eda-8e6a-4658-a2f7-71e8de53a5ff",
                                                "sense_id": "60a3ce98-f305-3be2-b33a-6d2438a7e445",
                                                "text": "Like rum, proper Batavia arrack from Indonesia, also known as arak or rack, is distilled from sugarcane. Unlike rum, it has a healthy dose of red rice added to the mash."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "664dec0d-c17e-4a3c-b796-30ebeb0e4c3d",
                                                "sense_id": "60a3ce98-f305-3be2-b33a-6d2438a7e445",
                                                "text": "Today, arrack is still produced and consumed in parts of Indonesia. It has a particular important position among the Hindus in Bali and Lombok, who use it in ritual and sometimes also in the non-ritual, secular context."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "223aba70-4e9b-3428-abe0-0d4491a30c9a",
                                        "entry_id": "b0d40755-cded-32e2-af4f-f671d1f12d1f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of arak (“aniseed-flavored alcoholic drink consumed primarily in the Middle East”)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "169a6247-442a-435c-8470-21acee0e721b",
                                                "sense_id": "223aba70-4e9b-3428-abe0-0d4491a30c9a",
                                                "text": "When he walked in and out, looking at the house in connection with the sun, the trees, and the lake, and said, rubbing his hands with might of heartiness, “Well done! Make the dowar now as ye well know, and to-night we will sweeten the bread with arrack, and the milk with honey, and at every fire there shall be a kid. […]”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b0d133a1-345e-4323-822e-e1be56a41d34",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d97d851-fa45-3967-a73a-d198120dba2e",
                        "source_sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Branntwein aus Reis oder Melasse",
                        "target_lang_word": "arak",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "arak",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f15c48ef-e65b-3bb4-8664-7bbc81d8aaca",
                                        "entry_id": "4f0ce0a4-68a4-3b2e-8ed0-a86f3fa3de8d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A clear, unsweetened aniseed-flavoured alcoholic drink, produced and consumed primarily in the Levant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d32d0378-b3fd-4413-a1f1-f6e1af61c5e6",
                                                "sense_id": "f15c48ef-e65b-3bb4-8664-7bbc81d8aaca",
                                                "text": "A rite of the grape harvest in the Christian villages dotting the Lebanon mountain range[…] is the perfectly legal distillation of homemade arak. This smooth, cool, refreshing liquor, tasting of licorice with a soupçon of peppermint, remains the staple drink at Sunday lunch, an eat-till-you-drop extravaganza of small meze dishes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4be088e-8101-4d90-999a-a326fca9a778",
                                                "sense_id": "f15c48ef-e65b-3bb4-8664-7bbc81d8aaca",
                                                "text": "In Lebanon they have arak, in Turkey raki, and they even make something similar in Saudi Arabia. This is not so surprising as the Arabs were probably the first people to distil alcohol; alcohol is an Arabic word. “Arak” means “sweat” in Arabic, and describes the distillation process rather than what happens when you drink too much."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4e9507f-bed7-3fbd-8c32-207982aeaab3",
                                        "entry_id": "4f0ce0a4-68a4-3b2e-8ed0-a86f3fa3de8d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative spelling of arrack (an alcoholic drink distilled from coconut palm flowers or sugar cane)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "alternative",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "arak",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33b88087-8312-3028-acee-d7a6a8bdbbed",
                                        "entry_id": "dda2cdfc-6447-3766-ac25-20f3f8870380",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A toothbrush tree (Salvadora persica)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4d1fd204-0e4b-481f-a5ce-c5aede46af52",
                                                "sense_id": "33b88087-8312-3028-acee-d7a6a8bdbbed",
                                                "text": "They use perfume freely, paint their eyes with kohl, and are constantly polishing their teeth with twigs of green arak-wood."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1e61159b-743d-4a55-a8e4-377804a2cb39",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d97d851-fa45-3967-a73a-d198120dba2e",
                        "source_sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
                        "source_sense_description": "Branntwein aus Reis oder Melasse",
                        "target_lang_word": "arak",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "arak",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "63f45c80-e4ad-3c02-8671-a67638dd9276",
                                        "entry_id": "a692ce61-a617-38bb-ad1e-49d816624a8f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Variante de arack."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3c0730ed-de21-4997-9661-bb7198aae09f",
                                                "sense_id": "63f45c80-e4ad-3c02-8671-a67638dd9276",
                                                "text": "L’arak, c’est la « boisson nationale » du Liban."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fea2046a-0f35-411b-94ba-bb643387c546",
                                                "sense_id": "63f45c80-e4ad-3c02-8671-a67638dd9276",
                                                "text": "Une pinte d’arak vous mettre l'âme en joie :"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d9ac3df-d472-453f-b43f-21df235bd0ba",
                                                "sense_id": "63f45c80-e4ad-3c02-8671-a67638dd9276",
                                                "text": "Beaucoup préféraient l’arak, la vodka ou le vin, mais je n’observai aucune attitude disgracieuse, les plus éméchés se contentant d’accompagner en sourdine les musiciens engagés par le maître de céans, un joueur de târ, un virtuose du zarb, un flûtiste."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3cf8406e-22b8-4449-b168-e14a48a6dc35",
                        "source_entry_id": "6d97d851-fa45-3967-a73a-d198120dba2e",
                        "source_sense_id": "9123a619-e7b8-3e69-8533-b2ddc8c8526c",
